@startuml launch_sequence
title paddock — sandboxed launch sequence (srt backend, v1)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

actor User
participant "Herdr" as Herdr
participant "cli.py" as CLI
participant "tui.py\n(chooser)" as TUI
participant "sessions.py\n(registry)" as Sessions
participant "profiles.py" as Profiles
participant "agents.py" as Agents
participant "backends/srt.py" as Backend
participant "synth_config.py" as Synth
participant "herdr_client.py" as Client
participant "srt\n(Seatbelt / bubblewrap)" as Srt

User -> Herdr : press prefix+c
activate Herdr
Herdr -> CLI : run `paddock` in a popup\nenv: HERDR_SOCKET_PATH,\nHERDR_ACTIVE_WORKSPACE_ID,\nHERDR_ACTIVE_PANE_ID
activate CLI
CLI -> TUI : run_chooser(cwd)
activate TUI

TUI -> Sessions : list live sessions
activate Sessions
Sessions --> TUI : name, backend, profile, attached tabs
deactivate Sessions
TUI -> User : Local / New sandbox session / Attach to existing?
User --> TUI : New sandbox session

alt Local namespace chosen
  TUI -> Client : tab create --cwd <cwd> --focus
  note right : plain tab, no session, no sandbox — flow ends here
else Attach to an existing session chosen
  TUI -> Sessions : look up chosen session
  note right
    msb: exec a shell into the running guest.
    srt: new process under the SAME settings
    file and workdir — shared policy and files,
    separate process tree.
  end note
end

TUI -> Profiles : load_profiles()
activate Profiles
Profiles --> TUI : built-ins + ~/.config/paddock/profiles/*.json
deactivate Profiles
TUI -> User : pick a profile (or build a custom one)
User --> TUI : profile

group Questionnaire (skipped when a saved profile is reused)
  TUI -> Agents : list registered agents
  TUI -> User : agent? tools? network? shared dir? skills? MCP servers?
  User --> TUI : answers
  TUI -> User : name this session?
  User --> TUI : session name
  opt user names the profile too
    TUI -> Profiles : save_profile(profile)
  end
end

TUI -> Sessions : register session\n(session_id, name, backend, profile,\nvm_handle, created_at)

TUI -> Backend : launch(profile, workdir)
deactivate TUI
activate Backend

Backend -> Backend : resolve workdir\n(shared_dir, or isolated scratch\nunder runs/<id>/work)
Backend -> Backend : build PATH shim dir runs/<id>/bin\n(symlink one binary per selected tool)
Backend -> Agents : layer-2 config for this agent\n(--settings JSON, .mcp.json + --strict-mcp-config, ...)
activate Agents
Agents --> Backend : agent flags + api_domains
deactivate Agents
Backend -> Synth : build synthetic config dir
activate Synth
Synth -> Synth : credentials for this agent only\n+ symlink whitelisted skills
Synth --> Backend : config dir path (-> CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR)
deactivate Synth
Backend -> Backend : write runs/<id>/srt-settings.json\nnetwork.allowedDomains (allowlist-only)\nfilesystem.allowWrite (workdir, run dir, /tmp)\nfilesystem.denyRead (~/.ssh, ~/.aws, ...)
Backend --> Client : pane command\n`srt --settings <file> "env PATH=<shim> <agent>"`
deactivate Backend

activate Client
Client -> Herdr : herdr tab create --workspace <id> --cwd <workdir>\n--label sbx:<session> --env CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=... --focus
Herdr --> Client : {"result":{"root_pane":{"pane_id":"wA:p2"}}}
Client -> Herdr : herdr pane run wA:p2 <command>
deactivate Client
CLI -> Sessions : record pane wA:p2 as attached
CLI --> Herdr : exit (popup closes)
deactivate CLI

Herdr -> Srt : start sandboxed process tree in pane wA:p2
deactivate Herdr
activate Srt
Srt -> Srt : enforce write paths, read denials,\ndomain allowlist (kernel-level)
Srt --> User : agent running in the sandboxed pane
deactivate Srt

note over Backend, Srt
  Tab creation and command execution are separate calls:
  the pane exists with the right cwd and label before any
  sandboxed process starts, so a launch failure leaves a
  visible, usable pane rather than a vanished window.
end note

@enduml
